## Where RD-11871 stands

**Goal:** the new **v1** EDI path in hedgehog (`pkg/hedgehog/api/v1` plus `service/payment` and `service/device`) currently sends **no lifecycle metrics**, and its `tenant_id` and `location_id` are always `unknown`. This ticket makes v1 send **the exact same 7 metrics as the legacy path** (RD-11676), with real tenant and location values. Legacy and v1 then add up together on the same dashboard.

**Stage:** the ticket is still in the **"Specify" phase**. It lists 9 design decisions to resolve before coding. As far as I know, no code exists yet.

| Dependency | Status | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| RD-11676 (legacy EDI lifecycle) | ✅ Merged | You reuse its metric names, tags and helper |
| RD-11872 / EDI-06 (legacy tenant and location via `HospitalRepository`) | ⚠️ In peer review | You share its repository and its lookup pattern. Coordinate with it, don't duplicate it. |
| RD-11679 issue metrics | Separate ticket | Pre-acceptance rejections go there, **not** here |
| **EDI metrics visible in Datadog** | ❌ Still unresolved | Doesn't block coding, but **blocks verifying in Datadog**. RD-11676's metrics weren't showing in QA. |

## The 9 decisions, with suggested answers to confirm with your lead

| # | Decision | Suggested answer |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | DogStatsD or OTel | **Option A, DogStatsD**, the ticket's recommendation. It guarantees identical series names. |
| 2 | `workflow_cancel` on v1 | **Out of scope; split into its own task.** Until then, a v1 device cancel counts as `workflow_failure`, as the ticket says. |
| 3 | Which JWT claims carry tenant and location | Needs code reading in `hbmiddleware` (the first prompt below finds them) |
| 4 | Not visible in your screenshots | Read it on the ticket |
| 5 | How the handler reaches the database | **Option A:** add a `HospitalRepository` field to `Handler`, and a nil repository means `unknown`. Use Option B only if RD-11872 lands first. |
| 6 | Is `locationId` the same as `hospital_id`? | Confirm from code and data with the lead |
| 7 | `location_id` grain | Follow whatever RD-11872 decides |
| 8 | Lookup failures | Already a requirement: warn-log, use `unknown`, never affect the request |
| 9 | Cache | **No cache for now,** or reuse RD-11872's cache if it adds one. Don't build a second one. |

